88}, {"text": "represents the historical, personal and literary contexts of this Romantic writer.\u201d", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.12354312354312354, "x1": 0.7593406593406593, "y1": 0.13675213675213677}, {"text": "How does this statement align with your understanding and appreciation of the conversations", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.1585081585081585, "x1": 0.8604395604395605, "y1": 0.1717171717171717}, {"text": "between the texts?", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.17637917637917638, "x1": 0.31978021978021975, "y1": 0.1864801864801865}, {"text": "In your response, make close reference to TWO of Keats\u2019 poems and to Campion\u2019s film Bright", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.21212121212121213, "x1": 0.8681318681318682, "y1": 0.22533022533022534}, {"text": "Star.", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.22921522921522922, "x1": 0.2153846153846154, "y1": 0.23931623931623933}, {"text": "f) Poetry and poetry", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.26495726495726496, "x1": 0.3208791208791209, "y1": 0.27816627816627815}, {"text": "\u201cPlath\u2019s and Hughes\u2019 poetry converse with tension despite some overlaps in the contexts of the", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.2999222999222999, "x1": 0.8736263736263736, "y1": 0.31313131313131315}, {"text": "poets.\u201d", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.3177933177933178, "x1": 0.23076923076923078, "y1": 0.331002331002331}, {"text": "How does this statement align with your understanding and appreciation of the conversations", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.35275835275835277, "x1": 0.8604395604395605, "y1": 0.36596736596736595}, {"text": "between the texts?", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.3706293706293706, "x1": 0.31978021978021975, "y1": 0.38073038073038074}, {"text": "In your response, make close reference to TWO of each poets\u2019 set poems.", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.40559440559440557, "x1": 0.7252747252747253, "y1": 0.4188034188034188}, {"text": "g) Shakespearean drama and prose fiction", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.45998445998445997, "x1": 0.49340659340659343, "y1": 0.4731934731934732}, {"text": "\u201cAtwood's novel Hag-Seed transforms, reimagines and reframes aspects of", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.47785547785547783, "x1": 0.7318681318681318, "y1": 0.49106449106449107}, {"text": "play the Tempest\u2019", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.49572649572649574, "x1": 0.3131868131868132, "y1": 0.508935508935509}, {"text": "How does this statement align with your understanding and appreciation of the conversations", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.5306915306915307, "x1": 0.8604395604395605, "y1": 0.5439005439005439}, {"text": "between the texts?", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.5485625485625486, "x1": 0.31978021978021975, "y1": 0.5586635586635587}, {"text": "End of Section 1", "x0": 0.42527472527472526, "y0": 0.8453768453768454, "x1": 0.5725274725274725, "y1": 0.8578088578088578}], [{"text": "Section Il - Module B: Critical Study of Literature", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.08857808857808858, "x1": 0.5681318681318681, "y1": 0.1048951048951049}, {"text": "20 Marks", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.11810411810411811, "x1": 0.1912087912087912, "y1": 0.1282051282051282}, {"text": "Attempt Question 2", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.1452991452991453, "x1": 0.2725274725274725, "y1": 0.1585081585081585}, {"text": "Allow about 40 minutes for this section", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.17249417249417248, "x1": 0.42747252747252745, "y1": 0.1825951825951826}, {"text": "Answer the questions on the paper provided", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.19968919968919968, "x1": 0.4703296703296703, "y1": 0.2128982128982129}, {"text": "Your answer will be assessed on how well you:", "x0": 0.13076923076923078, "y0": 0.22455322455322455, "x1": 0.46813186813186813, "y1": 0.24397824397824397}, {"text": "demonstrate an informed understanding of the ideas expressed in the text", "x0": 0.1912087912087912, "y0": 0.24475524475524477, "x1": 0.7296703296703296, "y1": 0.257964257964258}, {"text": "* evaluate the text's distinctive language and stylistic qualities", "x0": 0.16153846153846155, "y0": 0.26262626262626265, "x1": 0.6274725274725275, "y1": 0.27583527583527584}, {"text": "* organise, develop and express ideas using language appropriate to audience, purpose and", "x0": 0.16153846153846155, "y0": 0.27972027972027974, "x1": 0.8549450549450549, "y1": 0.29292929292929293}, {"text": "form", "x0": 0.1901098901098901, "y0": 0.29603729603729606, "x1": 0.2230769230769231, "y1": 0.3061383061383061}, {"text": "Question 2 (20 marks)", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.34032634032634035, "x1": 0.2934065934065934, "y1": 0.35353535353535354}, {"text": "Prose fiction", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.36752136752136755, "x1": 0.21978021978021978, "y1": 0.3776223776223776}, {"text": "a) Jane Austen\u2019s Emma is often regarded as her greatest novel.", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.3939393939393939, "x1": 0.5868131868131868, "y1": 0.40714840714840717}, {"text": "Explore how Austen creates her memorable characters to explore the issues of her time.", "x0": 0.14615384615384616, "y0": 0.4211344211344211, "x1": 0.7857142857142857, "y1": 0.43434343434343436}, {"text": "b) \u201cCharles Dickens is often considered the greatest novelist of the Victorian era because of his", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.4755244755244755, "x1": 0.8197802197802198, "y1": 0.4887334887334887}, {"text": "concern for both the individual and the broader social world.\u201d", "x0": 0.14505494505494507, "y0": 0.4933954933954934, "x1": 0.5868131868131868, "y1": 0.5034965034965035}, {"text": "With reference to at least TWO characters, explore aspects of Dickens\u2019 Great Expectations that", "x0": 0.14505494505494507, "y0": 0.5205905205905206, "x1": 0.8406593406593407, "y1": 0.5337995337995338}, {"text": "demonstrate this notion.", "x0": 0.14505494505494507, "y0": 0.5384615384615384, "x1": 0.31978021978021975, "y1": 0.5485625485625486}, {"text": "\u00a2) In An Artist of the Floating World, how does Kazuo Ishiguro create fascinating characters to explore", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.5920745920745921, "x1": 0.8758241758241758, "y1": 0.6052836052836053}, {"text": "the issues arising from his exploration of post-war Japan?", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.60994560994561, "x1": 0.5725274725274725, "y1": 0.6231546231546231}, {"text": "Poetry", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.655011655011655, "x1": 0.17142857142857143, "y1": 0.6682206682206682}, {"text": "d) \u201cTS Eliot's poetry reflects the Modernist vision with unrelenting bleakness.\u201d", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.6993006993006993, "x1": 0.7, "y1": 0.7125097125097125}, {"text": "How does this statement concur with your response to Eliot?", "x0": 0.15824175824175823, "y0": 0.7350427350427351, "x1": 0.5989010989010989, "y1": 0.7482517482517482}, {"text": "e) \u201cDavid Malouf poetry has an Australian flavour but engages in universal concerns.\"", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.77000777000777, "x1": 0.765934065934066, "y1": 0.7832167832167832}, {"text": "How does this statement concur with your response to Malouf?", "x0": 0.15714285714285714, "y0": 0.7972027972027972, "x1": 0.6153846153846154, "y1": 0.8104118104118104}], [{"text": "Drama", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.08857808857808858, "x1": 0.17142857142857143, "y1": 0.09867909867909867}, {"text": "f) \u201cDramatic texts create worlds of their own, allowing playwrights to explore the issues most central", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.11577311577311578, "x1": 0.8604395604395605, "y1": 0.128982128982129}, {"text": "to their vision of the world.", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.13286713286713286, "x1": 0.34175824175824177, "y1": 0.14296814296814297}, {"text": "How does this statement concur with your response to the play you have studied?", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.1686091686091686, "x1": 0.778021978021978, "y1": 0.18181818181818182}, {"text": "Non fiction", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.2128982128982129, "x1": 0.20659340659340658, "y1": 0.222999222999223}, {"text": "g) \u201cNon-fiction engages readers more powerfully than fiction.\u201d", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.2400932400932401, "x1": 0.5791208791208792, "y1": 0.2533022533022533}, {"text": "Explore the ways in which the non-fiction writer you have studied has used the form to engage", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.27583527583527584, "x1": 0.8681318681318682, "y1": 0.289044289044289}, {"text": "readers.", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.29292929292929293, "x1": 0.23736263736263735, "y1": 0.30303030303030304}, {"text": "Film", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.3473193473193473, "x1": 0.15384615384615385, "y1": 0.35742035742035744}, {"text": "h) \u201cClooney's Goodbye and Goodluck captures the essence of the contradictions of the McCarthy era", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.3745143745143745, "x1": 0.8703296703296703, "y1": 0.3877233877233877}, {"text": "but the issues it raises are ones which continue to concern us.\u201d", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.3923853923853924, "x1": 0.610989010989011, "y1": 0.4024864024864025}, {"text": "How does this statement concur with your response to the film?", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.4195804195804196, "x1": 0.6450549450549451, "y1": 0.43278943278943277}, {"text": "Media", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.473970473970474, "x1": 0.16703296703296702, "y1": 0.4840714840714841}, {"text": "i) \u201cUnfolding Florence\" explores ideas about the diversity of people's lives.\u201d", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.5011655011655012, "x1": 0.6824175824175824, "y1": 0.5143745143745144}, {"text": "How does this statement concur with your response to the documentary film?", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.5361305361305362, "x1": 0.743956043956044, "y1": 0.5493395493395493}, {"text": "Shakespearean Drama", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.5905205905205905, "x1": 0.2978021978021978, "y1": 0.6037296037296037}, {"text": "j) Asa history play, King Henry IV, Part 1 educates about the period in which it is set but it also", "x0": 0.11978021978021978, "y0": 0.6177156177156177, "x1": 0.8274725274725274, "y1": 0.6309246309246309}, {"text": "engages us in universal concerns.", "x0": 0.15164835164835164, "y0": 0.6355866355866356, "x1": 0.3956043956043956, "y1": 0.6487956487956488}, {"text": "How does this statement concur with your response to the play?", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.662004662004662, "x1": 0.6483516483516484, "y1": 0.6752136752136753}], [{"text": "The prescribed texts for Section II are:", "x0": 0.36043956043956044, "y0": 0.08857808857808858, "x1": 0.6384615384615384, "y1": 0.10178710178710179}, {"text": "+ Prose Fiction \u2014 Jane Austen, Emma", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.11577311577311578, "x1": 0.4021978021978022, "y1": 0.12742812742812742}, {"text": "- Charles Dickens, Great Expectations", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.14296814296814297, "x1": 0.4043956043956044, "y1": 0.1561771561771562}, {"text": "- Kazuo Ishiguro, An Artist of the Floating World", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.16938616938616938, "x1": 0.4747252747252747, "y1": 0.1825951825951826}, {"text": "+ Poetry -\u2014 T S Eliot, T S Eliot: Selected Poems", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.22377622377622378, "x1": 0.46483516483516485, "y1": 0.236985236985237}, {"text": "The prescribed poems are:", "x0": 0.1813186813186813, "y0": 0.25097125097125095, "x1": 0.37362637362637363, "y1": 0.2641802641802642}, {"text": "* The Love Song of J Alfred Prufrock", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.27505827505827507, "x1": 0.44945054945054946, "y1": 0.29448329448329447}, {"text": "* Preludes", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.30536130536130535, "x1": 0.2571428571428571, "y1": 0.31546231546231546}, {"text": "* Rhapsody on a Windy Night", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.33255633255633255, "x1": 0.3967032967032967, "y1": 0.3457653457653458}, {"text": "*The Hollow Men", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.35975135975135974, "x1": 0.310989010989011, "y1": 0.36985236985236986}, {"text": "* Journey of the Magi", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.38694638694638694, "x1": 0.3362637362637363, "y1": 0.40015540015540013}, {"text": "\u2014 David Malouf, Earth Hour", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.44133644133644134, "x1": 0.321978021978022, "y1": 0.452991452991453}, {"text": "The prescribed poems are:", "x0": 0.1813186813186813, "y0": 0.46853146853146854, "x1": 0.37362637362637363, "y1": 0.48174048174048173}, {"text": "* Aquarius", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.49572649572649574, "x1": 0.2571428571428571, "y1": 0.508935508935509}, {"text": "* Radiance", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.5229215229215229, "x1": 0.26153846153846155, "y1": 0.533022533022533}, {"text": "* Ladybird", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.5493395493395493, "x1": 0.2549450549450549, "y1": 0.5625485625485626}, {"text": "* A Recollection of Starlings: Rome '84", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.5765345765345765, "x1": 0.46373626373626375, "y1": 0.5897435897435898}, {"text": "* Eternal Moment at Poggia Madonna", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.6037296037296037, "x1": 0.45604395604395603, "y1": 0.616938616938617}, {"text": "* Towards Midnight", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.6309246309246309, "x1": 0.3230769230769231, "y1": 0.6441336441336442}, {"text": "* Earth Hour", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.6581196581196581, "x1": 0.2725274725274725, "y1": 0.6682206682206682}, {"text": "* Aquarius II", "x0": 0.1824175824175824, "y0": 0.6853146853146853, "x1": 0.2703296703296703, "y1": 0.6985236985236986}, {"text": "+ Drama \u2014 Henrik Ibsen, A House", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.7397047397047397, "x1": 0.41098901098901097, "y1": 0.7513597513597513}, {"text": "- Dylan Thomas, Under Milk Wood", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.7668997668997669, "x1": 0.378021978021978, "y1": 0.7801087801087802}, {"text": "+ Nonfiction - Edmund de Waal, The Hare with Amber Eyes", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.8212898212898213, "x1": 0.5648351648351648, "y1": 0.8344988344988346}, {"text": "- Nabokov, Speak, Memory", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.8484848484848485, "x1": 0.3901098901098901, "y1": 0.8616938616938616}], [{"text": "+ Film - George Clooney, Good Night, and Good Luck", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.08857808857808858, "x1": 0.5186813186813187, "y1": 0.10178710178710179}, {"text": "+ Media - Gillian Armstrong, Unfolding Florence", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.14296814296814297, "x1": 0.4714285714285714, "y1": 0.1561771561771562}, {"text": "+ Shakespearean Drama William Shakespeare, King Henry IV, Part 1", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.19658119658119658, "x1": 0.6450549450549451, "y1": 0.2097902097902098}, {"text": "End of prescribed texts for Section II", "x0": 0.36813186813186816, "y0": 0.25097125097125095, "x1": 0.6307692307692307, "y1": 0.2641802641802642}], [{"text": "Section Ill - Module C: The Craft of Writing", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.08857808857808858, "x1": 0.45494505494505494, "y1": 0.10178710178710179}, {"text": "20 Marks", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.11577311577311578, "x1": 0.1912087912087912, "y1": 0.1258741258741259}, {"text": "Attempt Questions 3a) and 3b)", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.14296814296814297, "x1": 0.35934065934065934, "y1": 0.1561771561771562}, {"text": "Allow about 40 minutes for this section", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.16938616938616938, "x1": 0.42747252747252745, "y1": 0.1794871794871795}, {"text": "Answer the questions on the paper provided", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.19658119658119658, "x1": 0.4703296703296703, "y1": 0.2097902097902098}, {"text": "Your answer will be assessed on how well you:", "x0": 0.13076923076923078, "y0": 0.22144522144522144, "x1": 0.46813186813186813, "y1": 0.24087024087024086}, {"text": "\u00a9 craft language to address the demands of the question", "x0": 0.16153846153846155, "y0": 0.24164724164724163, "x1": 0.589010989010989, "y1": 0.25485625485625485}, {"text": "_use language appropriate to audience, purpose and context to deliberately shape meaning", "x0": 0.1912087912087912, "y0": 0.2595182595182595, "x1": 0.8494505494505494, "y1": 0.27350427350427353}, {"text": "Read the extract below from \u201cMelbourne\u2019s Famous Water\" by Helen Garner:", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.30303030303030304, "x1": 0.676923076923077, "y1": 0.3162393162393162}, {"text": "In the last few weeks before | moved back to Melbourne, | had forgotten about time", "x0": 0.12307692307692308, "y0": 0.3581973581973582, "x1": 0.8582417582417582, "y1": 0.3714063714063714}, {"text": "and effort. There would be a five-day gap between \u2018uplift\u2019 and delivery. | decided to", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.37606837606837606, "x1": 0.856043956043956, "y1": 0.38927738927738925}, {"text": "drive down the Hume in a hire car loaded with immediate essentials \u2014 foam-rubber", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.39316239316239315, "x1": 0.856043956043956, "y1": 0.40326340326340326}, {"text": "strip, skin cream - and camp in the empty house till my stuff arrived.", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.411033411033411, "x1": 0.721978021978022, "y1": 0.42424242424242425}, {"text": "| slept badly on my foam rubber in the denuded flat and woke to a humid morning.", "x0": 0.12307692307692308, "y0": 0.4382284382284382, "x1": 0.8472527472527472, "y1": 0.45143745143745145}, {"text": "The sky was pearly, with a streak of amber cloud above the large, quiet old", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.4560994560994561, "x1": 0.7868131868131868, "y1": 0.4693084693084693}, {"text": "apartment blocks on the downward slope of Birriga Road. Kookaburras set up their", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.4731934731934732, "x1": 0.8626373626373627, "y1": 0.4864024864024864}, {"text": "jovial clamour. Way down on the golf course, sprinklers gushed in fountains all along", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.49106449106449107, "x1": 0.8714285714285714, "y1": 0.5042735042735043}, {"text": "the fairways. Sweating, looking neither left nor right, | loaded the hire car and headed", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.5081585081585082, "x1": 0.8769230769230769, "y1": 0.5221445221445221}, {"text": "for the highway.", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.5268065268065268, "x1": 0.26153846153846155, "y1": 0.54001554001554}, {"text": "Until Wangaratta the sky was covered in cloud the colour and texture of a water", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.554001554001554, "x1": 0.8274725274725274, "y1": 0.5672105672105672}, {"text": "biscuit; then it cleared. The day became a scorcher. The freeway was so wide and", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.5710955710955711, "x1": 0.8516483516483516, "y1": 0.5843045843045843}, {"text": "smooth and the landscape so flat and uneventful, that | kept blanking out. | had to", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.5889665889665889, "x1": 0.8461538461538461, "y1": 0.6021756021756022}, {"text": "eat lollies to stay alert. Once, | almost nodded off. | had slept well: | was not tired: |", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.6060606060606061, "x1": 0.8527472527472527, "y1": 0.62004662004662}, {"text": "knew | must be resisting something. But | want to go home, don\u2019t |?", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.6239316239316239, "x1": 0.7186813186813187, "y1": 0.6371406371406372}, {"text": "How drab the outskirts of Melbourne seemed when | took the exit. There was a", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.6487956487956488, "x1": 0.8219780219780219, "y1": 0.6697746697746698}, {"text": "whole new road system. | got lost in its flyovers and coloured shards and", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.668997668997669, "x1": 0.7670329670329671, "y1": 0.6822066822066822}, {"text": "incomprehensible signage. What had they done to my city? And had it always really", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.6860916860916861, "x1": 0.8637362637362638, "y1": 0.7000777000777001}, {"text": "been so...... flat?", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.7047397047397047, "x1": 0.27582417582417584, "y1": 0.7148407148407149}, {"text": "My new house, a single-fronted, single-storey terrace rented on a flying visit a month", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.7288267288267288, "x1": 0.8725274725274725, "y1": 0.7482517482517482}, {"text": "earlier, had bulged and shrunk in my memory. The whole building, like my spirits,", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.7498057498057498, "x1": 0.8395604395604396, "y1": 0.763014763014763}, {"text": "seemed sunken, unnaturally low.", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.7668997668997669, "x1": 0.41208791208791207, "y1": 0.7801087801087802}, {"text": "Question 3 a) 10 marks", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.8212898212898213, "x1": 0.3010989010989011, "y1": 0.8344988344988346}, {"text": "Continue this narrative in an imaginative piece of writing.", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.8484848484848485, "x1": 0.532967032967033, "y1": 0.8616938616938616}, {"text": "Aim to capture the style and the narrative voice of the extract and focus on the interior space of the new", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.8756798756798757, "x1": 0.8769230769230769, "y1": 0.8888888888888888}, {"text": "location.", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.8927738927738927, "x1": 0.1813186813186813, "y1": 0.9028749028749029}], [{"text": "Question 3 b) 10 marks", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.08857808857808858, "x1": 0.3021978021978022, "y1": 0.10178710178710179}, {"text": "Write a reflection in which you examine some of the textual features you have used to evoke the place", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.11577311577311578, "x1": 0.865934065934066, "y1": 0.128982128982129}, {"text": "and capture the voice of your piece. Consider how features from a prescribed text have influenced your", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.13286713286713286, "x1": 0.8747252747252747, "y1": 0.14607614607614608}, {"text": "choices.", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.15073815073815075, "x1": 0.18021978021978022, "y1": 0.16083916083916083}, {"text": "The prescribed texts for Section Ill are:", "x0": 0.35824175824175825, "y0": 0.2595182595182595, "x1": 0.6406593406593407, "y1": 0.2727272727272727}, {"text": "+ Prose Fiction - Kate Chopin, The Awakening", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.2867132867132867, "x1": 0.46813186813186813, "y1": 0.2999222999222999}, {"text": "\u2014 Elizabeth Harrower, The Fun of the Fair", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.3139083139083139, "x1": 0.42637362637362636, "y1": 0.32556332556332557}, {"text": "Franz Kafka, Metamorphosis", "x0": 0.13626373626373625, "y0": 0.3411033411033411, "x1": 0.34615384615384615, "y1": 0.3543123543123543}, {"text": "- Nam Le, Love and Honour and Pity and Pride and Compassion and Sacrifice", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.36752136752136755, "x1": 0.6967032967032967, "y1": 0.38073038073038074}, {"text": "- Colum McCann, Thirteen Ways of Looking", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.3947163947163947, "x1": 0.44505494505494503, "y1": 0.40792540792540793}, {"text": "McCann, What Time Is It Now, Where You Are?", "x0": 0.1879120879120879, "y0": 0.4188034188034188, "x1": 0.5373626373626373, "y1": 0.4397824397824398}, {"text": "-Rohinton Mistry, The Ghost of Firozsha Baag", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.4491064491064491, "x1": 0.46483516483516485, "y1": 0.46231546231546233}, {"text": "+ Nonfiction - Helen Garner, How to Marry Your Daughters", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.4972804972804973, "x1": 0.5582417582417583, "y1": 0.5104895104895105}, {"text": "Siri Hustvedt, Eight Days in a Corset", "x0": 0.13516483516483516, "y0": 0.5244755244755245, "x1": 0.4021978021978022, "y1": 0.5376845376845377}, {"text": "- George Omell, Politics and the English Language", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.5516705516705517, "x1": 0.4989010989010989, "y1": 0.5648795648795649}, {"text": "- Zadie Smith, That Crafty Feeling", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.5788655788655789, "x1": 0.37252747252747254, "y1": 0.5920745920745921}, {"text": "+ Speeches \u2014 Margaret Atwood, Spotty-Handed Villainesses", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.6278166278166278, "x1": 0.5637362637362637, "y1": 0.6410256410256411}, {"text": "\u2014 Geraldine Brooks, A Home in Fiction", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.655011655011655, "x1": 0.4021978021978022, "y1": 0.6666666666666666}, {"text": "- Noel Pearson, Eulogy for Gough Whitlam", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.6822066822066822, "x1": 0.43626373626373627, "y1": 0.6954156954156954}, {"text": "+ Poetry \u2014 Boey Kim Cheng, Stamp Collecting", "x0": 0.12197802197802197, "y0": 0.7303807303807304, "x1": 0.4593406593406593, "y1": 0.7435897435897436}, {"text": "\u2014 Gwen Harwood, Father and Child", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.7575757575757576, "x1": 0.3802197802197802, "y1": 0.7692307692307693}, {"text": "- Wallace Stevens, Thirteen Ways of Looking at a Blackbird", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.7847707847707848, "x1": 0.5593406593406594, "y1": 0.797979797979798}, {"text": "- Alfred Lord Tennyson, The Lady of Shallot", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.811965811965812, "x1": 0.44505494505494503, "y1": 0.8251748251748252}, {"text": "\u2014 Kate Tempest, Picture a Vacuum", "x0": 0.12087912087912088, "y0": 0.8383838383838383, "x1": 0.3769230769230769, "y1": 0.8515928515928516}, {"text": "End of paper", "x0": 0.45054945054945056, "y0": 0.8927738927738927, "x1": 0.5505494505494506, "y1": 0.905982905982906}, {"text": "8", "x0": 0.4956043956043956, "y0": 0.9300699300699301, "x1": 0.5032967032967033, "y1": 0.9386169386169386}]]